---
title: 'Scrollbar'
enterprise: true
---

The Scrollbar provides a familiar interface for panning around a chart, similar to native browser and operating system scrollbars.

Unlike the [Navigator](./navigator/), which allows both zooming and panning with resize handles, the Scrollbar is a pure panning control. This makes it ideal for users who are already zoomed in and need to navigate through their data.

## Enabling the Scrollbar

{% chartExampleRunner title="Scrollbar" name="scrollbar" type="generated" /%}

The Scrollbar is disabled by default. To enable it, add the following configuration:

```js format="snippet"
{
    scrollbar: {
        enabled: true,
    },
}
```

The Scrollbar appears when the chart is zoomed in. Use the [Zoom](./zoom/) feature to enable zooming, or set the initial zoom level using the [Chart State API](./api-state/).

## Visibility

The `visible` property controls when the Scrollbar is displayed:

-   `'auto'` (default) - shows the Scrollbar only when zoomed in
-   `'always'` - always shows the Scrollbar
-   `'never'` - hides the Scrollbar even when zoomed in

{% chartExampleRunner title="Scrollbar Visibility" name="scrollbar-visibility" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    scrollbar: {
        enabled: true,
        visible: 'always',
    },
}
```

## Vertical Scrollbar

By default, the Scrollbar appears horizontally at the bottom of the chart. A vertical Scrollbar can be configured for the y-axis.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Vertical Scrollbar" name="vertical-scrollbar" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    scrollbar: {
        enabled: true,
        vertical: {
            enabled: true,
            position: 'right',
        },
    },
}
```

The `position` can be set to `'left'` or `'right'` for vertical scrollbars, and `'top'` or `'bottom'` for horizontal scrollbars.

## Placement

The `placement` property determines whether the Scrollbar appears inside or outside the chart area:

-   `'outer'` (default) - positions the Scrollbar outside the chart, reserving space in the layout
-   `'inner'` - overlays the Scrollbar on top of the chart area

```js format="snippet"
{
    scrollbar: {
        enabled: true,
        placement: 'inner',
    },
}
```

## Customisation

The Scrollbar's appearance can be customised through its `track` and `thumb` properties.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Scrollbar Styling" name="scrollbar-styling" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    scrollbar: {
        enabled: true,
        thickness: 16,
        track: {
            fill: '#e0e0e0',
            cornerRadius: 8,
        },
        thumb: {
            fill: '#666666',
            cornerRadius: 8,
        },
    },
}
```

In this configuration:

-   `thickness` sets the height of horizontal scrollbars or width of vertical scrollbars
-   `track` styles the background area of the Scrollbar
-   `thumb` styles the draggable indicator showing the current viewport position

Both `track` and `thumb` support standard fill and stroke options including `fill`, `stroke`, `fillOpacity`, `strokeWidth`, and `cornerRadius`.

